The instance asks for Vulkan 1.1, not 1.2: a driver or loader that only has 1.1 (the PowerVR
GE8320 of the phones this port's armeabi-v7a build runs on, among others) refuses an instance
that asks for more with VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER. Everything above 1.1 was already optional
above: the timeline semaphores, dynamic rendering and the rest are probed per device and enabled
as extensions or core (the port's capabilities say which), the SPIR-V is 1.3 for such a device,
and VMA is told the same version. A 1.2 or 1.3 driver keeps working under a 1.1 instance: what it
has beyond 1.1 comes through the device and its extensions, the way emulators have always used
a lower instance version with newer devices.
--- a/plume_vulkan.cpp
+++ b/plume_vulkan.cpp
@@ -4506,7 +4506,7 @@
         appInfo.applicationVersion = VK_MAKE_VERSION(1, 0, 0);
         appInfo.pEngineName = "plume";
         appInfo.engineVersion = VK_MAKE_VERSION(1, 0, 0);
-        appInfo.apiVersion = VK_API_VERSION_1_2;
+        appInfo.apiVersion = VK_API_VERSION_1_1;
 
         VkInstanceCreateInfo createInfo = {};
         createInfo.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_INSTANCE_CREATE_INFO;
